cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite it and name the full Git commit ID or
  release tag you read. The specification changes; a citation without a commit
  does not identify what was cited. Cole Miller is the canonical editor, not
  the sole writer: much of the text was drafted with AI assistance, and each
  specification node and research note records the role AI played. Attribute
  a specific claim to the editor only where the provenance shows the editor
  made it.
title: "AI Pacing"
abstract: >-
  A Git-native, machine-readable specification of AI Pacing: slowing and
  conditioning the conversion of frontier AI capability into irreversible
  power while preserving bounded research progress and meaningful human
  vetoes. Includes the specification, its checks, a systems-engineering
  workspace, an evidence protocol, replications of external models, and
  research on an off-Earth pact.
authors:
  - family-names: Miller
    given-names: Cole
repository-code: "https://github.com/uncomposed/ai-pacing"
url: "https://ideas.proximitytoprogress.com/ideas/ai-pacing"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - AI safety
  - frontier AI
  - compute governance
